under the merged declaration (#5). Write-up: `docs/paper/diagnosis-clonal.md`; numbers: `benchmarks/results/diagnosis-clonal-2026-11-23.json`.\n\n- Declared outcome: D1 fails, so time structure of this kind does not explain the Sheih drop. With time-only clones, eta against the within-patient null stays at 0.013 or below, although that null's p over-rejects (15 to 18 of 40 against a bound of 6 at sigma 0.1). With real signal, eta against the time-point null keeps 99 to 100% of eta against the within-patient null.\n- Sheih per run, with clone-bootstrap intervals: recorded eta reproduces exactly; 'under half in 12 of 12' holds for the point estimates only (NHL-7 palantir and scfates_ppt intervals reach 0.62 and 0.77); the k-means lift is within +-0.05 as point values but not as intervals.\n- Daniel 2022 declined by the owner; not run.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shreyandhawa/clonal-trajectory-research/issues/8/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shreyandhawa/clonal-trajectory-research/issues/8/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]]